From: Jordan Hefner <jordan.hefner@vanbuskirkco.com> 
Sent: Wednesday, May 20, 2026 5:58 PM
To: Kelly Boyd <kelly.boyd@vanbuskirkco.com>
Subject: Re: financials

 

Myron's projects look the way they do because we sent final bills for 930, 940, 1000, 916 buildings last month so we are billing out our overhead and profit along with all final bills because those projects are done. We did keep some escrow held back on the projects that we closed out if they still have exterior work to be done, but we have build out overhead and profit. All of our labor and our equipment cost because the projects are completed other than escrow work.

 

The two projects for the townhomes that are still in process 908 through 9 14 and 900 through 906. Both of those projects are built very close to the actual currently.

 

164 Village Circle is showing underbuilt because Kara has not entered the settlement statement from our closing. Once she enters that settlement statement, it will show that it's been built to the full amount of the contract plus a few change orders.

 

I am planning on being more involved with the AFP process starting with these May AFP's.

I I'm trying to put the Project Manager that's in charge of the project in the driver seat on the AFP's but I'm hoping that I will have the bandwidth to be able to sit in on all of them going forward for a while. 

 

I'm definitely not gaming anything. We have some legitimate extraprofit on the townhomes because we were very frugal with our spend and we cut deals where we could.

We set those as fixed price jobs same as we do the rest of our projects and with us doing so many of them at one time we were able to get incredibly good deals on quite a bit of the project. We are showing good profit on those projects, but I totally understand if we need to defer some of that profit back to ownership since we did so much better on the projects. For outside clients, we obviously would not do that, We would just take the win on being under budget. 

 

Not trying to get anyone in trouble, honestly right now I'm trying to keep my head above water with all of the current projects and all of the new projects that we have coming.

I'm starting to see a light at the end of the tunnel, but I have a long ways to go training these two new people and getting houses ready to go in the ground.

 

Not a complaint, just letting you know where I'm at. 

 

Thanks,

Jordan Hefner

 

 

 

 

 

