From: Kelly Boyd <kelly.boyd@vanbuskirkco.com <mailto:kelly.boyd@vanbuskirkco.com> >
Sent: Wednesday, May 20, 2026 5:39:17 PM
To: Jordan Hefner <jordan.hefner@vanbuskirkco.com <mailto:jordan.hefner@vanbuskirkco.com> >
Subject: financials 

 

I know you are swamped but we need to figure out what’s going wrong.  I am using BuilderTrend/Financial/Invoices to get at Amount Paid. I am using BuilderTrend/Financial/Job Costing Budget to get at Actual Costs.  This should give us project actual costs vs what the client has paid. I pulled the data today.

 

These projects look good. We’re a little under billed for 164 Village Circle but otherwise ok.

 

R25022 Mapleton 3416 Bronze Lane

Actual Costs = $642K

Payments = $625K

 

R25027 171 Village Circle

Actual Costs = $633K

Payments = $634K

 

R25029 164 Village Circle

Actual Costs = $521K

Payments = $403K

 

I was under the impression we were under billing Myron to protect him, which would help explain the gross profit challenges on the income statement. It looks just the opposite though. We appear to be charging him much more than actual project costs. This is problematic as it both looks bad, and it will cause us to be short income later when the costs hit. And Gross Profit should look good now, but it doesn’t.

 

R25007 930 Norway 

Actual Costs = $717K

Payments = $735K

 

R25008 940 Norway 

Actual Costs = $653K

Payments = $779K

 

R25018 1000-1006 Riverstone 

Actual Costs = $729K

Payments = $913K

 

R25019 916-922 Riverstone 

Actual Costs = $716K

Payments = $900K

 

R25020 908=914 Riverstone

Actual Costs = $545K

Payments = $569K

 

R25021 900-906 Riverstone 

Actual Costs = $522K

Payments = $523K

 

I need you to be honest with me. Do you have visibility to how we are deciding what and when to bill clients? Are you gaming this a bit to try and make ends meet on the cash side? Or are you just so busy you haven’t had time to figure it out?  I don’t care what the answer is, I just need to know where you’re at with this.

 

The combination of gross profit looking terrible and then the actual project data saying you have overbilled Myron by close to $500K is going to get both of us in trouble. If this is a bandwidth issue, Brandi and I can dig in with Kara to see what is happening. I don’t think you are losing money, but our tracking and accounting isn’t good.

 

Thanks

Kelly Boyd

